格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"一个基于tv动画yumemita中的人物千石由乃，使用剧照素材，应用于deepseek-harness的自定义配色插件；A custom color scheme plugin for deepseek-harness, based on the character Yuno Sengoku from the TV anime \"Yumemita\"","id":"gh:1343705437","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"deepseek-harness-yunoseek","slug":"clclyzybzjsq/deepseek-harness-yunoseek","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"一个基于tv动画yumemita中的人物千石由乃，使用剧照素材，应用于deepseek-harness的自定义配色插件；A custom color scheme plugin for deepsee"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"k-harness, based on the character Yuno Sengoku from the TV anime \"Yumemita\""},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-yunoseek-skin"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Yunoseek pink skin for the DeepSeek Harness web GUI. It restyles the DSH browser UI with the pink ar"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"t direction of the yunoseek chat UI (`#E91E8C` / `#FF6B9D` gradients, pink tints) while reusing ever"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"y DSH layout and component unchanged, through the standard client-plugin interfaces:"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"- **Pink token layer** — a theme `overrideTokens` layer over the `--dsw-*` semantic tokens and the `"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"--dsw-static-deepseek-*` scale, every token carrying explicit light and dark values from yunoseek's "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"two palettes. The skin is always on and follows the user's light/dark/system preference; no settings"},{"id":"p4s4","text":" change needed.\n- **Art direction sheet** — the pink Hero glow recolor per palette, and the **assist"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"ant avatar** painted into every chat assistant row via its stable `data-chat-flow-kind` attribute (t"},{"id":"p4s6","text":"he host's CSS Modules class names are hashed and not addressable cross-package).\n- **Brand marks** ("},{"id":"p4s7","text":"non-`official` builds only) — the yunoseek logo in the sidebar brand row, the gradient \"Yunoseek\" wo"},{"id":"p4s8","text":"rdmark, and the welcome artwork in the conversation Hero seat. Official DeepSeek Harness composition"},{"id":"p4s9","text":"s already own those single-occupant slots with the built-in brand, so the skin yields them by defaul"},{"id":"p4s10","text":"t (see \"Build profile\" below).\n- **Yunoseek identity prompt** — the node half registers the yunoseek"},{"id":"p4s11","text":" system prompt (`assets/system-prompt.js`) as the first system-prompt section, so every assembled sy"},{"id":"p4s12","text":"stem prompt starts with the Yunoseek persona."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"extra system prompt takes ~1200 tokens and can be banned/started though the method written in releas"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ystem prompt takes ~1200 tokens and can be banned/started though the method written in release 0.2.0"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Yunoseek identity prompt"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Beyond the visuals, the plugin injects the yunoseek identity prompt into the model. Its node half re"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"gisters a `systemPrompt` section named `yunoseek:identity` with order `-200`, which renders **before"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"** the harness identity (`-100`) and the deployment persona (`0`) — the very first text the model re"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ads for every turn. The default text is the yunoseek system prompt from `assets/system-prompt.js`, e"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"mbedded at build time."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The injection is on by default and applies globally to every agent in the profile (the section lives"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" in the prompt registry's global layer). To disable it or replace the text, override the row from yo"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ur profile patch (`$DSH_HOME/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml`) — a later layer that replaces the row's"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" (`$DSH_HOME/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml`) — a later layer that replaces the row's `config` value:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Config is read at boot, so restart `dsh web` after changing it. The section text is static: it carri"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"es no `{{variable}}` references — a custom prompt containing `{{…}}` fails prompt assembly on purpos"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"e (fail loud keeps a malformed prompt out of the model request).\n**modified prompt takes about 1200 "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"eeps a malformed prompt out of the model request).\n**modified prompt takes about 1200 extra tokens**"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Requirements: a dsh installation (the `dsh` CLI) and a web profile — the default GUI profile is name"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ents: a dsh installation (the `dsh` CLI) and a web profile — the default GUI profile is named `web`."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### From GitHub"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"A git install fetches sources, not built artifacts, so pnpm runs the package's `prepare` script to b"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"uild `lib/`. pnpm ≥ 10 refuses to run a git dependency's `prepare` until explicitly allowed — the fi"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"rst `add` fails and dsh prints the exact package key; copy it into the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yam"},{"id":"p16s4","text":" `add` fails and dsh prints the exact package key; copy it into the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml`:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"then re-run the `add`. (That allowance is permission to execute the package's code at install time; "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"only allow packages whose source you trust, and pin a commit: `github:<owner>/dsh-yunoseek-skin#<sha"},{"id":"p18s3","text":">`.) Then (re)start your `dsh web` once so the new roster row composes; later code changes to the sk"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"in hot-reload through the web HMR chain."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### From npm or a tarball"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Prebuilt options need no build allowance:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Uninstall"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Build profile and the brand seats"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The tsdown config pins `DSH_CLIENT_BUILD_PROFILE` (default `official`). In an `official` build the s"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"kin applies the token layer, avatar sheet, and Hero glow **only** — official web compositions contai"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"n the built-in deepseek brand, which owns the `sidebar.brand.mark` / `sidebar.brand.name` / `convers"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"ation.hero.brand.mark` seats and must not collide. To show the yunoseek marks instead (e.g. a dev/se"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"lf-built web, or after disabling the built-in brand row), build with:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"and, when your composition still carries the built-in brand row, disable it in the profile patch (`$"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"DSH_HOME/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml`):"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Build"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The `prepare` script is self-contained (docs/user/develop/basic/publish.md): it builds from `src/` w"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ith a dedicated tsdown config — no monorepo context, no project references, no typechecking. Outputs"},{"id":"p31s3","text":": `lib/index.js` (ESM node half) and `lib/client.js` (CJS browser half)."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- The identity prompt is global and forward-most: a later layer that registers a `complete: true` sy"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"stem-prompt section replaces the whole prompt for an agent, and the injected text disappears there ("},{"id":"p33s3","text":"the registry's documented complete-section behavior).\n- Custom prompt text must not contain `{{…}}` "},{"id":"p33s4","text":"— prompt variables render strictly and an unknown reference fails assembly.\n- The assistant avatar i"},{"id":"p33s5","text":"s painted into chat rows by selector: `[data-chat-flow-kind=\"assistant-step\"]::before` with a fixed "},{"id":"p33s6","text":"34px geometry. If ui-conversation changes that attribute or row geometry, the rule (in `src/client/s"},{"id":"p33s7","text":"tyles.ts`) needs a revisit.\n- The sidebar and Hero marks are skipped in `official` builds by design "},{"id":"p33s8","text":"(single-occupant brand slots); see above for the dev-profile path.\n- The Hero glow rule targets `[da"},{"id":"p33s9","text":"ta-phase=\"hero\"] svg ellipse`; a future Hero redesign may move the glow out of an SVG ellipse."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
